nt": "lattice", "cell": [1.0, 4.0, 3, 120], "L": 10, "n_fires": 4269, "n_fires_candle_sampled": 329, "n_false_lock_all": 1047, "false_lock_rate_all": 0.24525650035137034, "wilson_ub_all": 0.25838785339946363, "n_priced": 102, "n_untradeable": 227, "untradeable_breakdown": {"no_qualifying_candle": 162, "no_candles": 37, "no_candle_after_signal": 28}, "untradeable_frac": 0.6899696048632219, "n_false_lock_priced": 72, "false_lock_rate_priced": 0.7058823529411765, "wilson_ub_priced": 0.7855364180782637, "ev_eq": {"n": 102, "mean": -0.5490196078431373, "G": 71, "df": 70, "se": 0.5842338886200114, "t": -0.9397257135150926, "ub979": 0.6612166701329063, "tcrit_bonf": 3.1972909505013414}, "ev_vw": {"n": 102, "mean": -1.9499820297665837, "G": 71, "df": 70, "se": 0.04581776476693038, "t": -42.55951899194373, "ub979": -1.855070861180167, "tcrit_bonf": 3.1972909505013414}, "n_days": 71, "n_stations": 22, "n_obs_1min": 67, "n_obs_routine": 35, "mean_cost_c": 28.92156862745098, "sum_entry_vol": 6093.410000000001}, {"variant": "lattice", "cell": [1.0, 4.0, 3, 120], "L": 20, "n_fires": 4269, "n_fires_candle_sampled": 329, "n_false_lock_all": 1047, "false_lock_rate_all": 0.24525650035137034, "wilson_ub_all": 0.25838785339946363, "n_priced": 98, "n_untradeable": 231, "untradeable_breakdown": {"no_qualifying_candle": 160, "no_candles": 37, "no_candle_after_signal": 34}, "untradeable_frac": 0.7021276595744681, "n_false_lock_priced": 69, "false_lock_rate_priced": 0.7040816326530612, "wilson_ub_priced": 0.7853681933021491, "ev_eq": {"n": 98, "mean": -0.5918367346938775, "G": 69, "df": 68, "se": 0.5577938655014952, "t": -1.0610312721201682, "ub979": 0.5642638035082286, "tcrit_bonf": 3.2009229789424904}, "ev_vw": {"n": 98, "mean": -2.6332762838376684, "G": 69, "df": 68, "se": 0.6032110615564333, "t": -4.365431026816992, "ub979": -1.3830426831366815, "tcrit_bonf": 3.2009229789424904}, "n_days": 69, "n_stations": 22, "n_obs_1min": 66, "n_obs_routine": 32, "mean_cost_c": 29.142857142857142, "sum_entry_vol": 5579.95}], "subgroups": [{"kind": "max", "E_position": "E fractional", "feed": "routine", "n": 2, "false_locks": 0, "rate": 0.0, "wilson_ub": 0.6576197725990219}, {"kind": "max", "E_position": "E==hi", "feed": "1min", "n": 863, "false_locks": 30, "rate": 0.03476245654692932, "wilson_ub": 0.04919137313690452}, {"kind": "max", "E_position": "E==hi", "feed": "routine", "n": 509, "false_locks": 337, "rate": 0.6620825147347741, "wilson_ub": 0.7018236083417704}, {"kind": "max", "E_position": "E==lo", "feed": "1min", "n": 865, "false_locks": 428, "rate": 0.49479768786127165, "wilson_ub": 0.5280655425706886}, {"kind": "max", "E_position": "E==lo", "feed": "routine", "n": 523, "false_locks": 52, "rate": 0.0994263862332696, "wilson_ub": 0.12806518491199304}, {"kind": "min", "E_position": "E fractional", "feed": "routine", "n": 7, "false_locks": 2, "rate": 0.2857142857142857, "wilson_ub": 0.641065548235854}, {"kind": "min", "E_position": "E==hi", "feed": "1min", "n": 714, "false_locks": 127, "rate": 0.17787114845938376, "wilson_ub": 0.20762217894674392}, {"kind": "min", "E_position": "E==hi", "feed": "routine", "n": 349, "false_locks": 19, "rate": 0.054441260744985676, "wilson_ub": 0.08345775738231048}, {"kind": "min", "E_position": "E==lo", "feed": "1min", "n": 637, "false_locks": 38, "rate": 0.059654631083202514, "wilson_ub": 0.08082067734229259}, {"kind": "min", "E_position": "E==lo", "feed": "routine", "n": 265, "false_locks": 92, "rate": 0.3471698113207547, "wilson_ub": 0.4063031808169328}], "headline": "Executed literally, the frozen spec produces **zero fires in all 8 cells x 3 latency arms**: brackets are 1 degF wide in (floor, cap) terms (a 2-whole-degree rung), so `lo+M <= E <= hi-M` is empty for M=1.0 and needs a half-degree extreme for M=0.5; observed extremes are whole degrees. No PASS is possible and I did not move any bar. Under the one charitable reading that lets the rule fire (exploratory 'lattice' variant, primary cell, 4,734 fires over the full universe) the finality inference is **wrong 1,125 times = 23.8% (Wilson UB 25.0%)** against a 2% / 5% bar. The cause is data-source disagreement, not timezone: IEM's day extreme differs from the official settlement value by 1 degF on about half of days, one-sidedly, and a rung is only 2 degF wide. Priced on a random 8% subsample of fired rungs (L=10): n priced 128, untradeable 65%, EV -0.34c/contract equal-weight (signed day-clustered t -0.27).", "choices": ["**Bracket geometry literal**: `[lo,hi] = [floor_strike, cap_strike]` exactly as carried on the rung. Widening it is the exploratory 'lattice' variant only (PASS-ineligible).", "**Signal timestamp** `t_sig = ts(obs_i) + 60 s` (strict `< t` look-ahead rule, anchor b). A build that uses `t_sig = ts(obs_i)` shifts every signal by 1 minute; immaterial at L>=10.", "**Reversed-and-held**: the last H=3 observations *including the current one* all satisfy `temp <= E(t)-R` (HIGH) / `>= E(t)+R` (LOW), with E(t) the running extreme at t. On 1-min feed H=3 means 3 minutes; on routine feed it means 3 METAR obs (~2-3 h).", "**Local day** = [round(close_time to hour) - 24 h, that hour], i.e. NWS standard-time midnight-to-midnight (see section 9). E accumulates from day start.", "**Terminal window** `close - W*60 <= t_sig <= close`; first qualifying t only; one fire per rung per cell.", "**Feed selection per market** (recorded in `signal.json: src`): 1-min if >=1000 of 1440 minutes AND >=65 obs in the last 130 min; else routine (`asos.py` report_type 3&4) if >=6 obs in the day and >=2 in the last 130 min; else the rung is skipped (8 rungs). Only a physical bound filter (-60..130 degF) is applied; no deployed-rule glitch filter.", "**Entry cost is `yes_ask`** for every fire (FINAL-YES always buys YES). For YES-settled rungs this equals the spec's winner-side cost. For false locks the spec's 'winner-side = 100 - yes_bid' is the NO price, which a YES buyer cannot pay; I charge the real YES ask and the loss `-(ask+fee)`. Using the winner-side cost for false locks would have *hidden* losses; the gate here is outcome-independent (deployable).", "**Entry** = first candle with `t_sig+L <= end_period_ts <= close_time`, `0 < yes_ask <= 98`, and `100-ask-fee > 0`; none -> UNTRADEABLE (candle-less rungs are counted untradeable, conservative). Candles are sparse (trade/quote-change minutes only), so 'first candle at or after' can be several minutes later.", "**EV**: per-contract net cents; equal-weight (one contract per fire, as the spec's accounting) and volume-weighted by the entry candle's traded volume. The Bonferroni t uses the day-clustered (CR1, linearised ratio) SE, df = G-1 (G = distinct local days); a PASS would have to clear the bar on BOTH weightings (the stricter reading of an ambiguous spec). One-sided 97.9% UB = mean + t_{0.979,G-1} * SE.", "**False-lock rate** is over ALL fires (a property of obs + official result), not just priced ones; the priced-only rate is also in the JSON.", "**Clusters** = local calendar day of the market."], "closing": "A PASS would have been necessary-but-not-sufficient; there is no PASS, so nothing here supports a canary. The program's 44th closed study (if Build A agrees) is not a failure of finality as an idea -- the descriptive table shows that where the extreme sits relative to the feed's one-sided bias changes the false-lock rate from ~50% to ~3-6% -- but that is an *outcome-informed* observation made on the same data, so it is a hypothesis for a new pre-registration with its own forward holdout, not a result. And even a ~3% false-lock rate is fatal at these prices: a winner buys at <=98c for +1c to +2c net, a loser costs ~98c, so break-even needs a false-lock rate near 1-2%; see the lattice EV rows for what the tape actually paid."}